WEBVTT

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.720
Universal Century 0001.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.380
To mark the space settlement program

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:10.260
that accompanied the increase
in population,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:13.930
the Earth Federation government
changed the calendar

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.050
from Anno Domini to the Universal Century.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.550
As the curtain rose on this new era,

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.680
Laplace, the prime minister's residence,
exploded.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.010
This was history's worst act of terrorism,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.340
carried out by
an anti-Federation organization.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:33.090
Of the perpetrators,
Syam was the sole survivor.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:35.510
And so, LaPlace's Box fell into his hands

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.590
and his life would be forever changed
because of it.

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.470
Almost a century has passed since then.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.340
Syam has become the head
of a mighty foundation,

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:47.840
and it's rumored that
the opening of Laplace's Box

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.510
could overturn the Federation.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.380
But Syam has decided to do just that,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.840
in order to break the stagnant status quo
of the times.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.800
Meanwhile Banagher Links,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.840
a student attending
the Anaheim Electronics Industrial College

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:09.550
at the colony Industrial 7,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.930
has a fateful encounter with
a green-eyed girl falling from the sky.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.630
She says her name is Audrey.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.510
She arrived at the colony via a ship
belonging to the Neo Zeon group

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.800
known as the Sleeves.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.050
When Banagher hears her story,

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.550
he no longer feels isolated
and out of place,

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:28.930
something he's struggled
with his whole life.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:32.090
Prevent it? Prevent what?

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.260
War.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.130
The girl's real name is Mineva Lao Zabi.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.630
Although she is an important figure
in Neo Zeon,

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.470
she seeks to prevent
the transfer of Laplace's Box.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:52.300
What the heck? I know this.
I've seen that image before.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.130
I see you're curious about that.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.720
Mineva does her best to talk Cardeas Vist,

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.840
the current head of the Vist Foundation,
out of it.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:05.550
But Cardeas rejects Mineva's proposal,

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:09.550
and goes on to negotiate
the handover of the Box to the Sleeves.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:14.260
If it's misused,
it could destroy the world.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.590
So you're going to give us
the key as a test, to start?

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.050
At this point, the Londo Bell
unit of the Earth Federation Forces

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.340
begins seizing control of the colony
to stop the handover of the Box.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:30.010
The negotiations break down
as the fighting spreads.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:34.130
Banagher wanders off in search of Audrey,

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:39.050
but instead finds himself face to face
with a white mobile suit.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.840
You've come this far;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.800
are you confident that
those feelings of yours will not waver?

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:47.840
The burden she bears is immense.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:51.930
Father!

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:56.970
Father...

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.260
I'm sorry, Mom.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.550
I must...

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:05.760
...go!

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.470
Cardeas,
who turns out to be Banagher's father,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:13.180
entrusts him with the Unicorn Gundam,
the key to Laplace's Box.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.720
As if responding to Banagher's own will,

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.800
it emits a crimson light
and fends off the Sleeves mobile suit.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:25.010
But as the battle ends,
Banagher loses consciousness,

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:29.800
and is retrieved by the Earth Federation
Forces warship the Nahel Argama.

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:08.470
(FULL FRONTAL'S PURSUIT)

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:14.720
Riddhe...

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.470
I want you to know you were lucky.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.880
Surviving doesn't mean you're a coward.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.180
Any more than dying means you were brave.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.550
The only thing
that separates the two is luck.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.630
Yes, Commander Norm.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.880
Attention approaching vessel,
you are ordered to halt immediately.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.380
This is the Nahel Argama
of the Federation Space Forces, Londo Bell.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:40.840
Your vessel
has crossed our defensive perimeter.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.930
Damned terrorists!

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.050
Wait.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:49.380
It's trash?!

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.760
It appears to be a wrecked Salamis class.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.130
Its reserve power supply is still alive.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.380
Seems the thermal sensors misidentified it.

00:05:56.340 --> 00:05:58.590
Cancel the alert. Return to your stations.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.720
And recall the mobile suits.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:01.800
Are you sure?

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.550
Is there a problem?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.930
It was just misidentified debris?

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.130
Yep. We're lucky
it wasn't an enemy out there.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.800
Enemies will appear though.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:17.010
They probably think that
we recovered Laplace's Box.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:21.300
And as long as that quad-wing
mobile suit is still kicking...

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:24.550
So this is no time
to wait for reinforcements.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.970
That's right.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:26.930
Have you gotten it open yet?

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.010
Well...

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:32.840
I didn't expect the system to be
so resistant to outside interference.

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:36.970
Meaning you weren't told anything
outside of your specific department?

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:37.930
Yes.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:41.260
Once the UC Project was placed under
the Vist Foundation's jurisdiction

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.090
the entire picture was never...

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.630
Hey! Enough chatter! Shut your mouth!

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.090
This line is closed.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.090
What's the UC Project?

00:06:55.630 --> 00:06:58.590
ECOAS can't investigate this by ourselves.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:00.010
If we did,

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:02.720
our guest from Anaheim would meddle
in it as if he were the top brass.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:12.050
The UC Project is a top secret program,
part of the E.F.S.F. Reorganization Plan.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.930
This Unicorn is the flagship.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.510
The entire body
uses psycho-frame technology,

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.470
which supplements the psycommu,

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:23.680
transmitting the pilot's psycho-waves
directly to the drive system.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:27.840
Which means the pilot can control it
just by thinking.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.090
But the pilot's body
can't really take that, right?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.380
No.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:36.180
But the NT-D is supposed
to have a time limit

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.010
of only 5 minutes once activated.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:39.630
This "NT-D" is...

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.340
Commander Daguza!

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:47.470
I told you that I should be present
when you're interrogating rescued staff!

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:48.930
Captain Otto.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.880
It would be wise for us
to leave this sector

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:52.470
with a single ship right now.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:58.630
Chances are the recovered Gundam type
has something to do with Laplace's Box!

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.470
Please set a course for Luna II
as soon as possible.

00:08:01.510 --> 00:08:02.720
That may be, but...

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:04.930
I agree, Captain!

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.880
But we shouldn't go to Luna II.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:11.180
We should head for
our Anaheim Electronics headquarters,

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.510
at Von Braun on the moon.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.840
Attention. Entering second deployment.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.130
Watch out for sections
under security lockdown.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.720
Wait here for now.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:24.550
You still don't know
who was piloting that Gundam?

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:27.680
We don't. Apparently the cockpit hatch
hasn't opened yet.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.090
It's you.

00:08:29.130 --> 00:08:30.220
Are you alright?

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.550
I'm the pilot who rescued you guys.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.800
My name's Riddhe Marcenas.

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:38.880
I'm Audrey Burne.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.680
Want to go check it out?

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:42.430
That Gundam.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:43.630
It's on your mind, isn't it?

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:44.840
Ensign Riddhe...

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.800
We'll be fine, Ensign Mihiro.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.260
I know a secret spot
where we can sneak a look.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.430
That's not what I meant.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:51.760
Yeah! Let's go!

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:54.010
This Nahel Argama

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:58.550
was the mothership of the Gundam Team
in the first Neo Zeon War!

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:01.970
This must be fate for it
to carry the new Gundam now!

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:03.510
Yeah.

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:05.380
Let's go, Micott. You're coming too!

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.130
I'm going too.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:17.630
If it hadn't been for that Gundam,
we would've all been annihilated.

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.930
I want to know who was piloting it, too.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.590
Unlike Luna II,
which is on the far side of the Earth,

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:27.630
the Moon is right next to us.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:30.760
The enemy will expect us
to head for the moon.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:34.130
We should set a course for Luna II,
even if it's a detour.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:38.680
We can get to the moon with
the resources we have left, can't we?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.590
I think the Commander is just impatient.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:44.260
Traveling with no hope of reinforcements,
I'll be even less patient.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.720
We're in this situation
because of civilians

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:49.760
who've put pressure
on the military chain of command.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.880
The duty of a soldier
is to carry out orders.

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:55.010
- Don't blame us for your failure.
- Cut the transmission.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:56.340
Now!

00:09:57.180 --> 00:10:00.050
I know ECOAS can do as they please
during an operation

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:03.300
but I wish they'd get off our backs
while we're giving them a ride.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:06.050
That goes for that high maintenance
executive from Anaheim, too.

00:10:06.090 --> 00:10:08.470
No use complaining if he can't hear you.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.880
That wreckage we encountered
has decelerated.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:17.380
Now traveling at relative velocity zero.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:20.300
Haunted by ghosts of the One Year War, eh?

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.680
Have the mobile suits eliminate it.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.630
They can push aside
something that size, no problem.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:26.090
But they've already returned.

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:27.260
What?

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:29.300
Those were your orders, sir.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:33.300
Do you want to order them to launch again?

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.970
Just blast it with the main guns!

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.800
Got it.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:50.260
Enemy's position confirmed.

00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:53.180
Transmit the coordinates to the Rewloola.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.970
Then let's wait and see what they do.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.470
That's a Gundam?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:03.630
That's what they say,
but it looks completely different.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.550
I feel like I've seen you somewhere before.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.010
I know!

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.430
Natsume Swanson, the actress!
Do people tell you that you look like her?

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.680
I don't know much about
the entertainment world, so...

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.470
Okay.

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:25.760
Hey, Mr. Ensign!

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.300
The hatch is opening!

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.470
Banagher?! Why're you- -?!

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:52.220
He doesn't look like a pilot!

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.590
Banagher!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:00.800
Banagher!

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:01.880
Doctor!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:05.380
Banagher...

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.010
Hey, are you okay?

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:10.760
Audrey...

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.880
Banagher, can you hear me?

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.180
If you can hear me,
squeeze my hand, alright?

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.880
Bridge, this is Mihiro.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.800
The boy's regained consciousness.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.840
Commander Daguza?!

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:26.380
I'd like to ask him some questions.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:28.010
The rest of you, leave. Now.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:29.090
Yes, sir, but...

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:31.510
At least let me finish
giving him his treatment.

00:12:32.050 --> 00:12:35.220
He still has no idea where he is.

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:37.300
You understand
that he's injured, don't you?

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:41.590
I understand this boy
hijacked a military mobile suit

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:43.800
and interfered in combat.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:47.430
It is a violation severe enough
to warrant capital punishment.

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:49.180
C-capital punishment...

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:52.430
He saved us, didn't he?

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:54.470
But with a stolen machine.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:12:59.310
We're ready to launch.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:02.890
Sit here and observe, Captain.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:07.180
This has got to be related
to Laplace's Box, huh?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:11.060
If this secret is so important
that they sent ECOAS to recover it...

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.930
There's a limit to how much
the Federation can mobilize in secrecy.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:19.140
Right now, they're likely in discussions
about how to handle it.

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:22.350
Talks between everyone responsible
who doesn't want the responsibility.

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:23.720
I hope you're right.

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:26.680
There's no sign of reinforcements,
is there? I assure you.

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:35.970
The Captain is going out today.

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:37.640
There won't be any work for us.

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:46.930
Can't say I'm convinced by that story.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:51.350
You say Cardeas Vist just handed that thing
over to a random boy like you?

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:54.890
And did he say anything else?

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.310
Like I said,
he told me to take the mobile suit

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.100
and use it to protect everyone.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.140
That's all.

00:14:03.010 --> 00:14:05.600
Would you believe me
if I told you he was my father?

00:14:15.510 --> 00:14:16.680
All units, scramble!

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:17.890
Turn about, full speed!

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:19.390
Quick! Get me a damage report!

00:14:19.430 --> 00:14:21.010
Anti-air surveillance!

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:22.310
No sign of enemies nearby!

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:23.430
Look harder!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.760
We were set up.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.510
This is because
you took too long to make a decision!

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:38.640
Cut it!

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:42.510
Intense heat sources
approaching at high speed.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.100
There are four total.
They're coming in from directly above!

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.060
What?! Missiles?!

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.680
Not likely. Their movement is...

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.010
I'd say mobile suits, but...

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:54.180
It's going through the debris.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.180
Unbelievable!

00:15:01.600 --> 00:15:03.970
The lead machine is approaching at

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.760
three times the speed of the others!

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.180
Let's see... Let's test the performance
of your new Gundam.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:15.680
All hands, prepare for anti-air combat!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:17.760
Are these the same guys
that attacked the colony?!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.310
I can't take this anymore!

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:20.260
Micott!

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.930
We've got to look for normal suits.

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:24.180
This ship could get a hole
blasted through it any minute now!

00:15:24.220 --> 00:15:25.720
Everyone! Put these on!

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:28.390
What happened to the other girl?

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:32.390
Interceptor system set to automatic fire!

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:34.810
Remaining enemy mobile suits
are still in flight!

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.640
You. Where do you think you're going?

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:38.890
Put on a normal suit and get to shelter!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.100
Anti-air defenses, what are you doing?

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.640
I can't get a lock on the- -

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:05.390
Just start firing!

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:11.850
Romeo 008 ready to launch!

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:13.970
Pilot to the mobile suit deck immediately!

00:16:16.010 --> 00:16:17.470
Here you go.

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.350
Thanks!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:23.470
You're awake now.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:26.180
It might save my life.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:27.810
This is my good luck charm.

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:29.060
You stay here and rest up.

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.810
There's nothing for you to do.

00:16:31.930 --> 00:16:34.810
We'll protect our own ship this time!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:38.310
A kid like that in control of a Gundam...

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:40.310
Banagher!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.560
Audrey.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.060
Banagher, listen to me...

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:50.010
That machine is registered
to your biometric data

00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:52.390
which means it can't operate without you.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:54.890
That's what I was told, but...

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:57.310
How do you know that?

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.640
Escape with me.

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.930
Rear main gun is damaged!

00:17:02.970 --> 00:17:05.560
Severe damage reported on
port side bulkhead seven.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.720
Ensign Mihiro to the bridge, now!

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.350
Damn these amateurs!

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:13.760
As long as they think we have the Box

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:17.970
they'll try to neutralize our ship
without hitting the engines.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.640
It's hard to believe that
a single mobile suit could...

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.140
That says...

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.430
This ship is carrying something

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:27.970
almost as important to them as the Box.

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.010
If we go now, we can get away.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:32.180
We can go back to Industrial 7.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:36.510
You sneak onto a cargo ship,
get to another Side, then go into hiding.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.060
And I'll figure out some way
to dispose of that machine.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.260
Audrey...?

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:43.640
If we don't...

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:46.100
That thing is just too dangerous.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:48.430
I can't let anyone get their hands on it.

00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:50.470
Wait a minute...

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:52.810
I'll explain more later.

00:17:52.850 --> 00:17:56.260
If you won't tell me anything,
how can you expect me to agree with you?

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:59.640
Don't try to sway me by talking like that.
It's not fair.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.930
What do you want to do?

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:07.260
Don't tell me what you should do.
Tell me what you want.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.810
Tell me what you truly want to do.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:12.140
And then I...

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:19.220
What are you- -?!

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:20.890
You know why I'm here?

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:26.560
Audrey!

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.350
Course is set!

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:32.350
Catapult hatches one through four, open!

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.010
Mobile suit corps,
get into position to launch.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:44.180
Are you getting scared, little man?

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:47.180
Nah, but I heard a squeak in your voice
just now, Lieutenant Homare.

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.810
There you go trying to start something.

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:53.350
Norm Basilicock.

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:54.810
Romeo 001, launch!

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:00.350
Galom Gorga. Juliet 002 launch!

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:03.310
Riddhe Marcenas.

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:05.180
Romeo 008. Here I go!

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:19.220
Severe damage reported on
port side catapult deck.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:20.350
Lieutenant Homare!

00:19:20.390 --> 00:19:22.100
Hurry up with the damage report!

00:19:22.140 --> 00:19:24.100
Get out of here
and go to the moon right now!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:26.390
Mr. Alberto,
it's dangerous for you to be in here!

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.760
That's the Sinanju! The Red Comet!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.260
There's no way you can defeat it.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:37.600
Two years ago, our experimental mobile suit
MSN-06S was stolen by Neo Zeon

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:41.720
while it was being transferred
from the lunar city Granada

00:19:41.760 --> 00:19:43.680
to a testing ground at Von Braun.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:48.140
The Federation Forces that were sent
to pursue it were wiped out instead.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.720
The primary culprit was...

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:54.970
Full Frontal,

00:19:55.010 --> 00:19:59.720
the man they call the Second Coming
of Char Aznable, the Red Comet.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:06.600
I've heard something like that.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.430
The "Ghost of Char",
who destroyed two Clop-class ships

00:20:09.470 --> 00:20:10.850
with a single mobile suit.

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:16.060
But Char went missing
during the Second Neo Zeon War.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:21.760
Anyway, we can't expect to beat him
with ordinary mobile suits.

00:20:21.810 --> 00:20:25.810
The Unicorn was made using data
collected with the Sinanju.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.680
We've got to get out of here now.

00:20:29.600 --> 00:20:32.100
Running away will leave us open
to attack from behind!

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.810
Transfer the verification data
to each section of the ship!

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.760
The enemy is not actually a ghost!

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:38.350
Send it to the mobile suit corps, too!

00:20:38.390 --> 00:20:39.760
You're an idiot without a clue.

00:20:39.810 --> 00:20:41.680
And you're the last person
I wanna hear that from!

00:20:55.930 --> 00:20:57.010
There it is!

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:07.140
Don't rush in, Ensign Riddhe.
Stay in formation.

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:11.100
Galom. Below you!

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.140
That can't be the real Char?!

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:20.350
Lieutenant Angelo...

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:23.470
There are multiple enemies.
We should at least provide some cover.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:26.890
No, we need only stand by, Ensign Sergi.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.850
We'd only get in the Captain's way.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.810
At this rate, everyone will...

00:21:39.850 --> 00:21:42.060
Attention, all attacking machines,
do you read me?

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:44.760
Cease fire immediately.

00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:47.560
We are holding Mineva Zabi
captive aboard this ship.

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:49.760
I repeat...

00:21:49.810 --> 00:21:52.600
We are holding the Zabi heir,
Mineva Lao Zabi,

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:54.180
captive aboard this ship.

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.720
If you do not
cease your attacks immediately,

00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:58.930
we cannot guarantee her safety.

00:21:58.970 --> 00:22:01.350
That girl is the Princess of Zeon?

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:06.010
We are prepared to begin negotiations,
and await your wise response.

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.470
Next time, on Mobile Suit Gundam Unicorn

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:44.260
CLASH WITH THE RED COMET,

00:23:45.100 --> 00:23:48.470
awaken the Newtype that lies within you.
